-- title:
--   Odd order of the Hasse square at supersingular places, p=3
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 5$ be a natural number with $3 \nmid M$, and let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $3$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\Omega$, that is: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$, together with a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the $q$-expansion of that form and whose reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\Omega$ to a Laurent series over $\Omega$ is nonzero. Work inside the intermediate field $\mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,\Omega\,M$ of $\Omega((q))$, the $\Omega$-subfield generated by the reduced ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(M)$. Let $\bar\jmath$ be an element of this field whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{jqModC}\,\Omega = q^{-1}\cdot$ (the reduction of $E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}$-numerator series), and let $b$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is $w.\mathrm{hasseRootFn}^2 = (\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\Omega\,w.\mathrm{series})^{-2}$. Let $v$ be a place of this function field over $\Omega$, i.e. a valuation subring containing $\Omega$, not equal to the whole field, and a principal ideal ring. Assume $\bar\jmath$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$ and that its residue value $v.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\bar\jmath \in \Omega$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,3\,\Omega$, the set of $j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with invariant $j$ has no nonzero point killed by $3$. Then $\gcd\big(2, |v.\mathrm{ord}\,b|\big) = 1$, where $v.\mathrm{ord}$ is the normalised additive valuation attached to $v$; equivalently, $\mathrm{ord}_v b$ is odd.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$3$ case of the statement that the square of the Hasse root function on the Igusa-type model of $X_1(M)$ has order coprime to $p-1$ at every supersingular place; in characteristic $3$ the Hasse invariant is itself this square, so the assertion is a parity statement on $\mathrm{ord}_v$. It is invoked in the proof of the general statement [`ModularCurve.gcd_sub_one_natAbs_ord_eq_one_of_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.gcd_sub_one_natAbs_ord_eq_one_of_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_pow), where the cases $p \ge 5$ are handled by the Deuring–Igusa data for $E_{p-1}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_gcd_two_natAbs_ord_eq_one_of_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_three_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_sq.lean

